{"step_index":451,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-07-11T12:32:36Z","thinking":"**Prioritizing Tool Usage**\n\nI'm now focusing on tool selection, emphasizing specific tools over general ones where possible. The goal is to optimize efficiency by leveraging tools tailored to particular tasks, like viewing files. This strategy promises a more targeted and less error-prone approach to problem-solving, which I will continue to refine and implement moving forward.\n\n\n**Refining Tool Choices**\n\nI'm now implementing strict tool selection based on recent updates, adhering closely to the rules outlined in critical instruction one and two. I will be avoiding direct manipulation of files using commands like `cat`, `grep`, `ls`, and `sed` inside bash commands; instead, I'm opting for specialized tools such as `grep_search`. I've made the updates.\n\n\n**Analyzing UI Logic Flaws**\n\nI've discovered a critical flaw in the UI design concerning language settings. Widgets built dynamically in `rows.py` only define `lang_id`, defaulting to `\"settings\"` for widgets lacking `lang_type`. Consequently, buttons without explicit `lang_type`—like `add_folder_btn`—are incorrectly evaluated as settings. This means they are getting treated as settings and not the strings defined directly in the YAML file! I've also found an issue wherein a raw ID not in `test_num.yaml` is not updated, contrary to expectations.\n\n\n**Investigating Text Translation Discrepancies**\n\nI'm now investigating why translated text may still appear as raw IDs in certain parts of the UI, specifically focusing on the difference between how tab text and other widget text are handled. I've realized that tabs, unlike other widgets, directly use `get_string` and that the absence of a direct call is likely responsible for their translation. I'll need to figure out where else the raw ID might appear.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":"false","Description":"\"Fix language update for ui_ keys\"","EndLine":"235","Instruction":"\"Change default lang_type inference to check for \\\"ui_\\\" prefix\"","ReplacementContent":"\"    def update_language_ui(self):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Dynamically update UI text for all widgets using ID linking.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        def walk_widget(w):\\n            lang_id = w.property(\\\"lang_id\\\")\\n            if lang_id:\\n                lang_type = w.property(\\\"lang_type\\\")\\n                if not lang_type:\\n                    lang_type = \\\"ui\\\" if str(lang_id).startswith(\\\"ui_\\\") else \\\"settings\\\"\\n                \\n                if lang_type == \\\"settings\\\":\\n                    new_text = self.get_ui_string(\\\"settings\\\", lang_id, \\\"label\\\")\\n                else:\\n                    new_text = self.get_string(lang_id)\\n                    \\n                if new_text and new_text != lang_id:\\n                    if hasattr(w, 'setText'):\\n                        w.setText(new_text)\\n                    elif hasattr(w, 'setTitle'):\\n                        w.setTitle(new_text)\\n            \\n            tooltip_lang_id = w.property(\\\"tooltip_lang_id\\\")\\n            if tooltip_lang_id:\\n                lang_type = w.property(\\\"tooltip_lang_type\\\")\\n                if not lang_type:\\n                    lang_type = \\\"ui\\\" if str(tooltip_lang_id).startswith(\\\"ui_\\\") else \\\"settings\\\"\\n                    \\n                if lang_type == \\\"settings\\\":\\n                    new_tooltip = self.get_ui_string(\\\"settings\\\", tooltip_lang_id, \\\"tooltip\\\")\\n                    label_text = self.get_ui_string(\\\"settings\\\", tooltip_lang_id, \\\"label\\\")\\n                    if label_text == tooltip_lang_id:\\n                        label_text = \\\"Settings\\\" # generic fallback if no label\\n                else:\\n                    new_tooltip = self.get_string(tooltip_lang_id)\\n                    label_text = \\\"\\\"\\n                    \\n                if new_tooltip and new_tooltip != tooltip_lang_id:\\n                    if hasattr(w, 'setToolTip'):\\n                        if lang_type == \\\"settings\\\" and label_text:\\n                            w.setToolTip(f\\\"<b>{label_text}</b><hr>{new_tooltip}\\\")\\n                 \n<truncated 68 bytes>","StartLine":"207","TargetContent":"\"    def update_language_ui(self):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Dynamically update UI text for all widgets using ID linking.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        def walk_widget(w):\\n            lang_id = w.property(\\\"lang_id\\\")\\n            if lang_id:\\n                lang_type = w.property(\\\"lang_type\\\") or \\\"settings\\\"\\n                \\n                if lang_type == \\\"settings\\\":\\n                    new_text = self.get_ui_string(\\\"settings\\\", lang_id, \\\"label\\\")\\n                else:\\n                    new_text = self.get_string(lang_id)\\n                    \\n                if new_text and new_text != lang_id:\\n                    if hasattr(w, 'setText'):\\n                        w.setText(new_text)\\n                    elif hasattr(w, 'setTitle'):\\n                        w.setTitle(new_text)\\n            \\n            tooltip_lang_id = w.property(\\\"tooltip_lang_id\\\")\\n            if tooltip_lang_id:\\n                lang_type = w.property(\\\"tooltip_lang_type\\\") or \\\"settings\\\"\\n                if lang_type == \\\"settings\\\":\\n                    new_tooltip = self.get_ui_string(\\\"settings\\\", tooltip_lang_id, \\\"tooltip\\\")\\n                    label_text = self.get_ui_string(\\\"settings\\\", tooltip_lang_id, \\\"label\\\")\\n                else:\\n                    new_tooltip = self.get_string(tooltip_lang_id)\\n                    label_text = \\\"\\\"\\n                    \\n                if new_tooltip and new_tooltip != tooltip_lang_id:\\n                    if hasattr(w, 'setToolTip'):\\n                        if lang_type == \\\"settings\\\":\\n                            w.setToolTip(f\\\"<b>{label_text}</b><hr>{new_tooltip}\\\")\\n                        else:\\n                            w.setToolTip(new_tooltip)\"","TargetFile":"\"/home/bimatkeo/Documents/Translator/Bimatkeo_Translator/app/core/desktop/main_window.py\"","TargetLintErrorIds":"[]","toolAction":"\"Fix update_language_ui\"","toolSummary":"\"Fix main_window.py update logic\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
