3:   ignore_bubble:\n84:     label: 'Ignore Small Bubbles:'\n85:     tooltip: Ignores any detected text bubbles smaller than this pixel area. Useful for filtering out noise or tiny sound effects.\n86\n<truncated 129 bytes>\non difficult fonts, but is slightly slower.\n89:   text_threshold:\n90:     label: 'Text Threshold:'\n91:     tooltip: How confident the detector must be to mark an area as 'text'. Lower values find more text but may include noise.\n92:   box_threshold:\n93:     label: 'Box Threshold:'\n94:     tooltip: How confident the detector must be to finalize the bounding box around the text. Higher values create tighter, more precise boxes.\n95:   unclip_ratio:\n96:     label: 'Unclip Ratio:'\n97:     tooltip: How much to expand the detected text box to capture outlines or parts of speech bubbles. Too high can cause boxes to merge.\n98:   det_rotate:\n99:     label: Detect Rotated Text\n100:     tooltip: Enables detection of vertically or rotated text within a bubble.\n101:   det_auto_rotate:\n102:     label: Auto-Rotate Image\n103:     tooltip: Automatically rotates the entire image if it's detected to be sideways before processing.\n104:   det_invert:\n105:     label: Invert Image Colors\n106:     tooltip: Inverts the image colors (black to white and vice-versa) before detection. Useful for white text on black backgrounds.\n107:   det_gamma_correct:\n108:     label: Gamma Correction\n109:     tooltip: Applies gamma correction before detection. Can improve detection on certain image types.\n110:   min_text_length:\n111:     label: 'Min. Text Length:'\n112:     tooltip: Ignores any recognized text shorter than this length. Useful for filtering out noise or single characters.\n113:   prob:\n114:     label: 'OCR Prob. Threshold:'\n115:     tooltip: Minimum confidence for an OCR result to be accepted. Leave blank for automatic backend default.\n116:     placeholder: 'e.g., 0.85 (default: auto)'\n117:   inpainter:\n118:     label: 'Inpainter Model:'\n119:    