{"step_index":1638,"source":"MODEL","type":"RUN_COMMAND","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-07-11T15:18:01Z","content":"Created At: 2026-07-11T15:18:01Z\nCompleted At: 2026-07-11T15:18:02Z\n\n\t\t\t\tThe command completed successfully.\n\t\t\t\tOutput:\n\t\t\t\t# Bimatkeo Translator - Planning and Path Resolution Rules\n\nThese rules are immutable. All AI agents operating on this repository must read,\n understand, and strictly adhere to these rules in every conversation.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Rule of Planning First (Quy tắc Lập Kế hoạch Trước)\n- **NO GUESSING AND DIRECT EDITING:** Do not guess the user's intent or make ass\numptions about the codebase when an error occurs.\n- **PLANNING MANDATORY:** You must not edit any files or run modifying commands\nwithout first writing a plan (`implementation_plan.md`), marking it for feedback\n (`request_feedback = true`), and obtaining the user's explicit approval.\n- **NO BYPASSING:** Even if a request seems trivially simple, do not bypass the\nplanning process unless the user explicitly tells you that no plan is needed.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Rule of Path Resolution (Quy tắc Giải quyết Đường dẫn)\n- **RELATIVE PATH DESIGN:** The application is designed to resolve configuration\n and resource paths relative to `self.project_base_dir` (which represents the pr\noject's root folder).\n- **NO ABSOLUTE PATH FALLBACKS:** Never introduce absolute path calculations (su\nch as `os.path.abspath(__file__)` or directory-climbing fallbacks) to resolve pa\nth issues in UI components or builders.\n- **PRESERVE DESIGNS:** Keep `self.project_base_dir` intact as resolved by the m\nain window constructor. Do not attempt to re-initialize it or check alternative\nabsolute paths at the component level.\n\n---\n\n## 3. NoneType Path Joining Errors (Xử lý lỗi TypeError trong os.path.join)\n- **ROOT CAUSE ANALYSIS:** When a `TypeError: join() argument must be str, bytes\n, or os.PathLike object, not 'NoneType'` error occurs during path joining, the r\noot cause is typically that the relative configuration file name (e.g., `file_na\nme` loaded from `info.get(\"default\")`) is resolving to `None` / `null` from the\nconfiguration schema.\n- **CORRECT FIX\n<truncated 2467 bytes>\nprocess/multiprocessing decoupling code logi\nc. Avoid polluting global scope.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Rule of Underspecified Requirements (Quy tắc Hỏi Rõ Ràng - *Inspired by tr\nailofbits/ask-questions-if-underspecified*)\n- **NO ASSUMPTIONS ON AMBIGUITY:** If a user request lacks critical details (e.g\n., edge cases, API parameter specifics, or failure fallbacks), the AI MUST expli\ncitly ask for clarification before writing code.\n- **EXACTNESS IN TRANSLATION LOGIC:** For any new features interacting with the\ntranslation pipeline (CT2, LLM chains), do not guess token chunking or prompt sc\nhemas; propose a structure and ask the user to confirm.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Rule of Automated Testing Awareness (Quy tắc Tư duy Kiểm thử - *Inspired b\ny testmu-ai/pytest-skill*)\n- **TESTABILITY FIRST:** When implementing core logic (such as context profile m\nerging or UI configs), write the functions such that they are decoupled and easi\nly testable (e.g. using `pytest`).\n- **MOCKING & FIXTURES:** Keep in mind that features like OpenAI/Gemini API call\ns and local offline translations will require mocks/stubs during future test pha\nses. Design classes with dependency injection or clear boundaries to facilitate\nthis.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Rule of Skill Evolution (Quy tắc Tự Tiến hóa Kỹ Năng)\n- **REFERENCE SKILLS FIRST:** Before executing any task, creating any plan, or m\nodifying any code, the AI **MUST** internally reference and read the relevant gl\nobal skill files located in `/home/bimatkeo/.gemini/antigravity-ide/skills/` (su\nch as `python-ai`, `rust-tui-development`, `self-evolution`, etc.) during its pr\nocessing phase. Do not wait for the user to remind you or inject the context int\no the prompt.\n- **ALWAYS ON EVOLUTION:** Skill evolution is an 'always on' background process.\n Based on user chats, error resolutio\n Based on user chats, error resolutions, or when the AI fails to recognize a con\ntext, it must proactively self-evolve by extracting the lessons learned and upda\nting the respective skill files to adapt to the new reality.\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
